senses.gloss:
शरणा_गत (तः-ता-तं)
a. Refugee;
seeking shelter or protection.

शरण्ड (ण्डः) 1.
m. A bird; a rogue;
a lizard; an ornament; a lecher.

शरण्यु (ण्युः) 2.
m. A cloud; wind;
protector.

शर-भ (भः) 1.
m. A fabulous animal
with eight legs; young elephant;
monkey in
Rāma's army; camel;
locust; grasshopper.

शराव (वः) 1.
m. A lid; a measure;
shallow cup or dish.

सारसन (नं) 1.
n. A woman's zone;
a military belt.

शरीर-ज (जः) 1.
m. Sickness;
Kāma;
a son.
a. Of the body.

शारुक (कः-की-कं)
a. Mischievous;
noxious.

शार्कक (कः) 1.
m. The froth of milk;
lump of meat; candied sugar.

शार्ङ्गिन् (र्ङ्गी) 5.
m. An archer;
Viṣṇu.

सरित् (त्) 5.
f. A river in general;
thread.

स-रोध (धः) 1.
m. Loss, destruction;
opposition.

सर्प-भुज् (क्) 5.
m. A peacock, crane;
large snake.

सर्व्वेश (शः) 1.
m. A supreme lord;
the supreme being.

सर्व्वेश्वर (रः) 1.
m. Shiva; Viṣṇu;
a universal monarch.

सार्थवत् (वान्-वती-वत्)
a. Meaning;
numerous.
